00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:42.620
A deterministic compiler then emits dialect-specific SQL for skew-light, big query, or snowflake.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:51.340
The approach achieved 94.15% execution accuracy on the Spider-2 snow benchmark using Gemini 3 pro.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:57.180
Developers facing complex enterprise schemas can examine the released code for the constrained

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:04.960
think-act loop and semantic model query design. Okay, let's pop the hood on resolution adaptive KV

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:11.540
cache approaches. Everyone talks about KV cache compression as if it is a simple eviction problem.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:20.320
In practice, CKV treats context as entropy-guided semantic spans stored across a GPU CPU hierarchy

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:26.980
instead of discarding tokens outright. Each span keeps a lightweight summary vector on GPU

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:34.700
for fast routing while a low-rank SVD basis lives on CPU for on-demand reconstruction of individual

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:41.300
tokens. A trained zoom-in step selectively materializes only the spans relevant to the current

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:48.320
query, avoiding full cache reloads. This design trades a small amount of added latency for the

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:57.040
ability to handle 128,000 contexts with 53% less GPU memory than full caching. The quality gain

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:02.680
comes from preserving information that pure eviction methods lose permanently once a token is dropped.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:09.080
Teams running long-context agents should test resolution adaptive approaches when memory pressure

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:16.000
is the binding constraint rather than raw throughput. Testshot scrapers new YAML-driven video mode

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:21.480
on a web app you are documenting to see how quickly you can produce consistent feature demos.

